<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raymond Westerling</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1987">1987</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raymond Westerling was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> army officer, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>, who led counter-insurgency operations in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> in 1946–1947 that killed thousands of Indonesians. After leaving the army he formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> of Ratu Adil (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance">APRA</a>) and in January 1950 led an attempted coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandung">Bandung</a> against the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, killing dozens of soldiers. The coup failed, and he escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raymond-westerling.jpg" alt="Raymond Westerling" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministerie van Defensie · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raymond_Westerling.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
